1
00:00:00,079 --> 00:00:03,299
The roof on your RV costs the most and gets protected the least.

2
00:00:03,339 --> 00:00:07,539
This is an RV roof cover, sized twenty-one by ten feet.

3
00:00:07,679 --> 00:00:10,079
It only covers the roof, not the whole RV.

4
00:00:10,219 --> 00:00:13,019
No heavy tarp to wrestle with by yourself in the wind.

5
00:00:13,099 --> 00:00:15,799
The fabric is a heavy-duty 210 denier weave.

6
00:00:15,899 --> 00:00:19,159
It holds up against rain, snow, and sun all winter long.

7
00:00:19,299 --> 00:00:22,139
You strap it down with the drawstring at the edge.

8
00:00:22,199 --> 00:00:24,619
It stays put even when the wind really kicks up.

9
00:00:24,719 --> 00:00:26,659
One person can do it alone.

10
00:00:26,760 --> 00:00:28,519
No one needs to hold the other end.

11
00:00:28,639 --> 00:00:32,380
When it's not in use, fold it into the included storage bag.

12
00:00:32,419 --> 00:00:34,180
No room taken in the storage compartment.

13
00:00:34,279 --> 00:00:37,540
A simple way to protect the most expensive surface on your RV.
